  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 530.13, when the projected misstatement ($55,000) exceeds the tolerable misstatement ($50,000), the auditor should conclude there is an unacceptably high risk of material misstatement. AU-C 530.14 directs the auditor to consider expanding the sample, requesting management to investigate and adjust, or performing alternative procedures.
Wrong (B): Accepting results because individual sample misstatements were small ignores the requirement to evaluate the projected misstatement against tolerable misstatement.
Wrong (C): Ignoring the projected misstatement and relying on other procedures without first evaluating the sampling results violates AU-C 530.13.
