-- Q1648: Audit Sampling [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 530.A20–A21, when the auditor finds misstatements in a sample, the auditor must project those misstatements to the entire population and consider an allowance for sampling risk. The projected misstatement plus the allowance is compared to tolerable misstatement to evaluate whether the account may be materially misstated.
Wrong (A): Considering only the actual dollar amount found in the sample without projection would understate the likely total population misstatement.
Wrong (B): Projection of misstatements is required regardless of whether statistical or nonstatistical sampling was used, per AU-C 530.13.
Wrong (C): Assuming the sample is perfectly representative ignores sampling risk—the sample may not capture all misstatements in the population.$EXPL$
