-- Q1651: Audit Sampling [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AU-C 530.A19, for monetary unit sampling projection, the tainting percentage equals the misstatement divided by the recorded value: $1,000 / $5,000 = 20%. The projected misstatement is the tainting percentage multiplied by the sampling interval: 20% × $25,000 = $5,000.
Wrong (A): $1,000 is merely the actual misstatement amount found; MUS requires projecting through the tainting percentage, not using the raw misstatement.
Wrong (B): $25,000 would result from applying a 100% tainting to the full sampling interval, which would only apply if the entire recorded value were misstated.
Wrong (D): $20,000 does not correspond to any valid application of the tainting calculation for this scenario.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1651;

